  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Three strategic documents and operational guidelines developed and put in place
The national dialogue process Roadmap charted out (including agenda setting, priorities, timeframe, etc.)
The # and type of timely and strategic activities supported by UNDP</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1 Baseline - New Commission assumed a nationally owned dialogue process with few institutional/operational structures and conditions in place
Output 1.2 -Baseline -None</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two capacity-building training/workshops to commissioners along with demand-driven support to launch the operations of the ENDC 
A Communication Strategy, a National Dialogue Covenant, and two operational manuals and procedures
6 Prioritized activities</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP&#x2019;s support to the ENDC has been technical and financial. Major contributions of this support include: three years project was formulated providing a framework for the continuous support of UNDP and other partners to the project; a project Trust Fund has been established facilitating the fund mobilization and management activities on behalf of ENDC; Donor Roundtable Meetings were conducted and were helpful to accelerate the fund for the project; partnerships were established with International NGOs that are experienced to provide technical support on national dialogue to ENDC; Vehicles and IT Equipment were provided; and recruitment of 15 key technical staff was facilitated to strengthen the operational capacity of ENDC. 

As a result of the direct implementation of the 2022 AWP, the institutional gaps of ENDC have been significantly improved. ENDC&#x2019;s Strategic Plan (2015-17EC), Communication and Media Strategy, internal procedure, policies, and organizational structure developed and put into force. The ENDC website has also been developed and soon will be operational. 

With regards to the launching of the national dialogue, good progress on the preparatory works of the national dialogue has been accomplished by ENDC. Fifteen consecutive consultative workshops with 1380 participants (Male 1150 and Female 230) from different segments of society were conducted to collect feedback on the dialogue methodologies and approaches as well as identify root causes of differences. Criteria/parameters were developed and consulted for the identification of participants, facilitators, and conveners. Partnerships with CSOs and the Media are established. Mapping of 1300 Woredas and negotiation with universities (who will be hosting the regional offices) was completed to facilitate the national dialogue at the local and regional levels. ENDC has also started its public outreach and awareness creation activities to increase public confidence in the processes of the national dialogue.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
